# Files that must NOT reach the public internet.
#
# The publish directory is build/ — the compiled React app. Everything else
# in this folder is working material: the source, the dependencies, the local
# environment file and the build scripts. None of that belongs on the
# internet, and the local .env must never be published.
#
# This is the publish-side lock. .gitignore is the repo-side one. Both must
# agree: .gitignore decides what Netlify uploads, .netlifyignore decides what
# Netlify publishes.
#
# The same file is copied into build/ by scripts/prepare-publish.mjs, so a
# hand-dropped build/ folder is protected the same way.

# --- source trees, never part of the published app ---
src/
public/
scripts/
node_modules/

# --- build config, not served content ---
# netlify.toml is deliberately NOT excluded: a hand-dropped build/ folder
# needs it at its root for Netlify to apply the SPA fallback and the /api/*
# proxy. It holds no secrets — only the public backend hostname.
package.json
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
jsconfig.json
craco.config.js
postcss.config.js
tailwind.config.js
components.json
.gitignore
.netlifyignore
README.md

# --- secrets and local config ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
*token.json*
*credentials.json*
*.pem
*.key

# --- logs & OS noise ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
